Proc.query is used for read-only operations that can be safely re-executed on retry without side effects. The following Sol code demonstrates using Proc.afterCommit to queue a structured process specification:

```sol
Proc.query {
  let x = Proc.afterCommit {
    // x is queued for the transaction
    Proc.afterCommit {
      // x is queued for the transaction
      Proc.afterCommit {
        // x is queued for the transaction
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This rule ensures that Proc.runNow does not block the caller while the script is being executed. The script must be executed as a top-level function, such as `Proc.runNow`, to ensure it executes immediately and returns a result that is not lost or lost.

```sol
Proc.runNow {
  // This function is part of the top-level function call
  // and is not part of the top-level function call
}
```
